checks_run.procedure:
Confirm the frozen candidate before reviewing:
- git rev-parse HEAD in the repository;
- the diff from the source commit to HEAD outside docs/delivery;
- the candidate ID recomputed in the repository tree, and in a complete, non-shallow clone at the source commit and at HEAD;
- the same again after the run, because other reviewers' runs auto-commit evidence.

Attack the round-4 mechanisms.

(1) Read every catch, finally, .catch and Promise in the 7-file closure and in decimal.js 10.6.0.

(2) NEW swallow-probe.mjs: a real string code generation on the exercised round-3 S1 path, with six ways of handling its failure:
- W1: empty catch;
- W2: finally { return; };
- W3: unhandled Promise rejection;
- W4: Promise .catch(() => undefined);
- W5: rethrow wrapped with `cause`;
- W6: W5 at evaluation time.
Each form goes through lint, the scan, the no-codegen run and the unit-node control.

(3) A closure-parser probe X1: a string-named export specifier, `export { "x" as y } from "../scoring.ts"`.

(4) Does the internal-failure rule cover every fuzz.test.ts outcome check? (read)

(5) The API effect of the EvalError rethrow: probe E mocks @mth/shared/calc so that a marked expression throws a real EvalError, then POSTs /benefit-formulas/validate and /benefit-formulas. The real engine cannot throw EvalError without the flag, and Fastify cannot run under it.

Confirm that the engine's formula results are unchanged:
- re-run probe C (my round-1 formula fuzz, unchanged; sha256 8d9a21f7…) in unit-node and in unit-formula-nocodegen (with the canary and regression tests), on Node 22 and Node 24;
- diff the engine's non-comment code lines.

checks_run.actual:
Probe C passes:
- unit-node: 65/65 on Node 22 and Node 24;
- unit-formula-nocodegen: 75/75 on both (65 + 10 canary/regression).
It covers:
- C1 injection strings;
- C2 limits;
- C3 division by zero is Unknown;
- C4 20,000-string fuzz;
- C5 an exact oracle: 3,000 random trees, stored result = oracle rounded half-up to 6 dp;
- C6 hostile inputs objects.

The engine's only non-comment code change (diff-scan D5) is the four `if (e instanceof EvalError) throw e;` lines, plus `catch {` → `catch (e) {` in value.ts.

(grep calls the probe-C logs 'binary' only because a C1 test name contains a NUL byte.)

Files outside docs/delivery:
- ADR-0024 and p3-work-split.md;
- eslint.config.js (formula blocks only);
- in packages/shared: codegen.nocodegen.test.ts, evaluate.ts, formula.test.ts, fuzz.test.ts, index.ts and value.ts.

No file under apps/, packages/db, openapi, vitest.config, package.json or the lockfile changed (D2: grep exit 1).

The web uses formatDecimal widely, and its behaviour is unchanged for every input except an EvalError, which cannot arise outside a refused code generation. The API EvalError path is a generic 500 (SEC-R4-16).

checks_run.procedure:
The P3 surface, as in round 1, re-verified on this candidate:
- every P3 mutation: authorization re-checked at commit time, validation, If-Match, audit, no I/O inside a transaction;
- separation of duties and no on-behalf decision;
- the G1 agreements guard;
- dependency-graph cycle refusal and its concurrency;
- the advisory-lock registry;
- decimals;
- migrations 0020–0027;
- the contract (270 operations live, every p3-pending empty);
- the inheritedApproval annotation.

The API, web, db and worker are unchanged since round 3 (diff-scan D2), so my round-1 static review stands. Confirmed through the suites, probes B and D, and static sweeps.

checks_run.actual:
Counts in each integration run:
- commit-time/BE18A tests: 30 (round 3: 30);
- aud-write-deny: 146;
- g1-agreements: 7, including 403/409 precedence and the migration-0025 COMMIT guard;
- SoD (submitter, on-behalf, proposer): 7;
- cycle/lock/concurrency: 32, including 'two DATABASE connections inserting A→B and B→A concurrently: exactly one commits';
